@tradition reading-corner
// Reading corner (0.60.7, the user's pick): on Sunday afternoons crew bring a book to the bow lounge armchairs and read
// together quietly, with a few murmured recommendations.
k: 452
title: Reading corner
when: weekly sunday
at: 16:00-17:00
min: 20
jitter: 10
where: 3 room Bow lounge: lounge-seat
hold: 1
who: quiet-corner 60%, window-seat 35%, lounge-regular 30%, everyone 10%
anim: read
from: The bow lounge

== mail
- Reading corner tomorrow, {time}, in the bow lounge armchairs. Bring a book. Talking is optional, and quiet.

== ask
- Reading corner this afternoon. I'm halfway through a mystery. No spoilers.   #funny
- Bring a book to the lounge later? It's quiet and the chairs are good.   #warm

== here
- Shh. Good bit.   #funny
- You'd like this one. Borrow it after.   #warm
- Just one more chapter.

== thanks
- You settle into an armchair with a book. Pages turn around you; somebody passes you a recommendation on a scrap of paper.   #warm

== chatter
- Reading corner got me through three novels this month.   #warm
- Sunday afternoon in the lounge with a book. That's the good life.   #warm
